:name: oveRTOS CMocka suite on STM32F746 — zero-heap
:description: Boot the oveRTOS test firmware on Renode's stm32f7_discovery-bb platform, capture CMocka output over semihosting, exit on SYS_EXIT_EXTENDED.

using sysbus

# `$bin` is set by the test harness via `-e '$bin = @<path>'` before this
# file is included.  Fallback path for standalone invocation mirrors the
# CMake build layout.
$bin?=@output/tests/renode-stm32f746-freertos-zeroheap/ove_test_renode_stm32f746_freertos_zeroheap.elf

mach create "stm32f746"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f7_discovery-bb.repl

sysbus LoadELF $bin

# Semihosting — the firmware uses `bkpt #0xab` with SYS_EXIT_EXTENDED
# (see tests/framework/semihosting_exit.h) and printf-to-semihosting via
# --specs=rdimon.specs in the link line.  The stm32f7_discovery-bb
# platform doesn't attach a SemihostingUart by default, so wire one up
# and route its output to the host console.
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "uartSemihosting: UART.SemihostingUart @ cpu"

# SPI.SPILoopback echoes every byte transmitted on the SPI bus back as
# the received byte — perfect for exercising the full ove_spi_*  →
# HAL_SPI_*  →  STM32SPI  →  loopback chain end-to-end.  The Renode
# stm32f7_discovery-bb platform doesn't attach a real SPI peripheral, so
# we layer the loopback on spi1 here.  test_renode_stm32_periph.c's SPI
# test relies on this peripheral being present.
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "spi1_loopback: SPI.SPILoopback @ spi1"

# Route the SemihostingUart output to a file so the outer harness can
# grep for the CMocka summary after the run.  $uart_out is set by the
# harness via -e '$uart_out = @/tmp/....log' before this script is
# included; fallback below supports manual invocation.
$uart_out?=@/tmp/renode-stm32f746-freertos-zeroheap.uart
cpu.uartSemihosting CreateFileBackend $uart_out true
# Mirror the same stream to the Renode console for live visibility.
showAnalyzer cpu.uartSemihosting

# Renode's own log for diagnostics.  Path is $rlog (harness-supplied).
$rlog?=@/tmp/renode-stm32f746-freertos-zeroheap.renode.log
logFile $rlog

# test_renode_stm32_obs::test_external_irq_trigger registers an EXTI
# rising-edge handler on PA0 early in the test run.  Schedule the
# stimulus so it fires inside that test's wait window.
#
# Renode has no built-in scheduled-event primitive in .resc, so we use a
# nested `emulation RunFor` sequence instead: run far enough that the
# common-suite runner reaches the obs suite (~3 sim-seconds), drive the
# pin, then run to the wall-clock cap.
emulation RunFor "00:00:03"
sysbus.gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 true
sysbus.gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 false
emulation RunFor "00:00:57"
